+/*
+ * HOST (18.13, experiment): call a definition that the emulator holds (written
+ * in C) over its own space of variables, not over the space of the program.
+ * One copy to SYS carries the request: the record (arg = the number of the
+ * definition) and right after it, in the same copy, the argument bits (the
+ * payload, as the data of EXEC). The emulator puts the payload at the start
+ * of its own space (the place the definition is set to read: values, or an
+ * image of cells), runs the definition and returns its results by copying:
+ * the image of the result (as many bits as the definition makes) to the
+ * position off[31:0] of the program space, and the 32-bit return value (numeric)
+ * to the position off[63:32]. The positions are given by the call; the emulator
+ * knows nothing of the layout of the data of the caller. The results are in
+ * the program space from the next tick (the same rule as for the answer of
+ * SYS). Answer: status 0, EINVAL (unknown definition, short payload, a result
+ * that does not fit), EFAULT (a result position outside the space). chan, flags: unused.
+ * 18.15: a definition may also give a displacement (bits) that is added to off[31:0]: a
+ * position inside a slot of 64 bits that it knows from the payload (fill of an unaligned
+ * address). The definitions: 0 clashes of a row with the rows of a layer, 1 fill, 2 encode
+ * of a layer, 3..10 the binary words + - and or xor = < u< (the value is the return
+ * value). The calls are allowed to any program.
+ * 18.16: 11 put (the n <= 128 bytes of the memory of the source, from the slot of its address, as a contiguous
+ * image at a bit address: the sink of the kernel), 12 cmove (the same bytes as an image at the slot of the
+ * destination, displacement 8 * (dst mod 4)), 13 numeric (the bytes of a 32-bit value, numeric, nb <= 8, laid as
+ * cmove). Diagnostics (development, 7.2.21): a call of HOST or of LONG that ends with a status other than 0
+ * (EINVAL, EFAULT, EBADF, EIO) writes "emulator: HOST <definition> failed: status <n> (<text>) at tick <t>"
+ * (LONG: "LONG space <s>") to stderr and stops the emulator with the exit code 3. The intervals the emulator
+ * writes as the result of a call (the image and the 32-bit value) are given by sys_host_results() to the audit of
+ * the checked emulator, which sees them as ranges of the tick.
+ */
+XOP(HOST,  7)
 /* reserve: SPAWN, POLL, MMAP, ... */
 
 XFIELD(req, op,    8)
